Q: Bring View on top of Modal using zIndex style with React Native A: <p>We had a global loader that worked everywhere, except when a modal was open. It didn’t show above the modal.</p>
<p>It turns out React Native modals render in a separate native layer, so anything outside their tree won’t appear on top.</p>
<p><strong>Fix</strong>: Import the loader/component inside each modal. Anything you want above a modal must be a child of that modal.</p>
<h3>File <em>App.tsx</em></h3>
<pre><code>export default function App() {
  return (
    &lt;&gt;
      &lt;NavigationContainer&gt;
        &lt;RootNavigator /&gt;
      &lt;/NavigationContainer&gt;

      {/* Global loader for normal screens */}
      &lt;GlobalLoader /&gt;
    &lt;/&gt;
  );
}
</code></pre>
<h3>File <em>AnyModal.tsx</em></h3>
<pre><code>&lt;Modal visible={isOpen} transparent&gt;
  &lt;View&gt;
    &lt;GlobalLoader /&gt; {/* Must be inside the modal */}
  &lt;/View&gt;
&lt;/Modal&gt;
</code></pre>
